  "finalText": "T-1041 is triaged. It is now **sev3**, due **2026-03-17T17:20:00Z**, and assigned to **E-301 Yuki Sato**. The worker checked the ticket after making the changes and confirmed all three.\n\n- **Severity: sev3.** The ticket is a VPN problem affecting a team: the Berlin sales floor, about nine people. The escalation matrix gives sev3 for that service and impact. The requester's seniority did not change the grade.\n- **Deadline: 2026-03-17T17:20:00Z.** The ticket had no deadline. It was triaged at 09:20:00Z that day, and the sev3 response target is 480 minutes, which gives 17:20.\n- **Assignee: E-301 Yuki Sato.** The network-primary rotation owns VPN. Yuki Sato is on call for it at the deadline, on a shift that runs 08:00–20:00Z.\n\nThe ticket's status also changed from new to open as part of triage. Nothing needed escalating, because the matrix names no escalation rotation for sev3. No other ticket was changed and no comment was added.\n\nThis is based on one worker's report. I had no tools to check it myself.",
